{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:94500","published":"2026-11-03T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-04T16:45:02.633802593Z","related":["CVE-2026-102266","CVE-2026-102267","CVE-2026-102268","CVE-2026-102271","CVE-2026-102272"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-102266","CVE-2026-102267","CVE-2026-102268","CVE-2026-102271","CVE-2026-102272"],"summary":"Critical: fence-agents security update","details":"The fence-agents packages provide a collection of scripts for handling remote power management for cluster devices. They allow failed or unreachable nodes to be forcibly restarted and removed from the cluster.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * pyjwt: pyjwt: Authentication bypass via empty HMAC key acceptance (CVE-2026-102266)\n  * pyjwt: PyJWT: Authentication bypass via improper public key validation (CVE-2026-102268)\n  * pyjwt: PyJWT: Authentication bypass via acceptance of DER public keys as HMAC secrets (CVE-2026-102271)\n  * pyjwt: pyjwt: Verification key substitution via unvalidated JWKS redirects (CVE-2026-102267)\n  * pyjwt: pyjwt: Token forgery via improper Unicode byte-order mark handling (CVE-2026-102272)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"fence-agents-aliyun","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/fence-agents-aliyun"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.10.0-110.el9_8.8"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux9/ALSA-2026:94500.json"}},{"package":{"name":"fence-agents-all","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/fence-agents-all"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.10.0-110.el9_8.8"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux9/ALSA-2026:94500.json"}}